      "name": "MIL-STD-2073 Decoder",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "MIL-STD-2073 Packaging Decoder",
        "intro": "<p>Packaging requirement codes on a military contract can look like alphabet soup, but each one carries specific instructions about materials, preservation, and marking. MIL-STD-2073 defines this coding system, and a single wrong character can mean rejected shipments or costly rework.</p><p>Royco Packaging developed this decoder so contractors, packers, and quality teams can translate these codes into plain language in seconds. This helps them quickly source materials that meet the required specifications. Programs across the Navy, Army, and Defense Logistics Agency reference MIL-STD-2073 in their packaging requirements. Accurate translation can help avoid delays and other downstream issues.</p><p>Enter the packaging requirement code from your contract, drawing, or DD Form 2326 into the tool below for an instant, plain-language translation, along with links to materials that meet each requirement.</p><p>Prefer the full document? You can download a <a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0659/3059/2478/files/MIL-STD-2073-1E.pdf?v=1787891611\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"View the full MIL-STD-2073 specification\">copy of the spec here</a>.</p>",
        "collection_root": "/collections",
        "product_root": "/products",
        "text_size": 17,
        "color_bg": "#ffffff",
        "color_panel": "#f6f7f9",
        "color_ink": "#14181f",
        "color_muted": "#5c6673",
        "color_accent": "#1f4e79",
        "color_line": "#d9dee5",
        "padding_top": 48,
        "padding_bottom": 48,
        "disclaimer": "<p>Decoded text is reproduced from MIL-STD-2073-1E w/CHANGE 4, Appendix J, Tables J-I through J-X. This tool is provided for reference only. Always verify against the current revision of the standard at the DLA ASSIST database and against the requirements of your specific contract or drawing.</p>"
      }
