    "decoder_content_1": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What MIL-STD-2073 Packaging Codes Tell You"
          }
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>MIL-STD-2073 packaging requirement codes pack a surprising amount of information into just a few characters. A single code points to a specific combination of preservation method, packing level, and unit container requirement drawn from Appendix J of the standard.</p><p>Missing even one digit can change the code's meaning. This can cause problems during a Defense Contract Management Agency inspection or lead to a rejected delivery. Contractors working with the Department of Defense, NASA, or major aerospace suppliers use these codes to keep documentation consistent across the supply chain.</p><p>This decoder pulls straight from the current standard, so the translation matches what an inspector expects to see. Packaging teams, buyers, and quality assurance staff use it to confirm a code before ordering materials. Packagers can use it to double-check a shipment before it leaves the dock.</p>"
          }
        },
        "button": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
            "button_label": "Explore MIL-STD-2073 Packaging Solutions",
            "button_link": "shopify://pages/mil-std-2073"
          }
        }
      },
